---
---If set to `true`, the available power output is based on the [FluidPrototype::fuel\_value](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/FluidPrototype.html%23fuel_value#fuel_value). Otherwise, the available power output will be based on the fluid temperature and [FluidPrototype::heat\_capacity](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/FluidPrototype.html%23heat_capacity#heat_capacity): `energy = fluid_amount * (fluid_temperature - fluid_default_temperature) * fluid_heat_capacity * effectivity`
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/FluidEnergySource.html%23burns_fluid#burns_fluid)
---@field burns_fluid? boolean
---@
---
---Property is only used when `burns_fluid` is `true` and the fluid has a [fuel\_value](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/FluidPrototype.html%23fuel_value#fuel_value) of `0`, or when `burns_fluid` is `false` and the fluid is at its `default_temperature`.
---
---In those cases, this property determines whether the fluid should be destroyed, meaning that the fluid is consumed at the rate of `fluid_usage_per_tick`, without producing any power.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/FluidEnergySource.html%23destroy_non_fuel_fluid#destroy_non_fuel_fluid)
---@field destroy_non_fuel_fluid? boolean
---@
---
---`1` means 100% effectivity. Must be greater than `0`. Multiplier of the energy output.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/FluidEnergySource.html%23effectivity#effectivity)
---@field effectivity? double
---@
---
---All standard fluid box configurations are acceptable, but the type must be `"input"` or `"input-output"` to function correctly. `scale_fluid_usage = true`, `fluid_usage_per_tick`, or a filter on the fluidbox must be set to be able to calculate the fluid usage of the energy source.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/FluidEnergySource.html%23fluid_box#fluid_box)
---@field fluid_box FluidBox
---@
---
---The number of fluid units the energy source uses per tick. If used with `scale_fluid_usage`, this specifies the maximum. If this value is not set, `scale_energy_usage` is `false` and a fluid box filter is set, the game will attempt to calculate this value from the fluid box filter's fluid's `fuel_value` or `heat_capacity` and the entity's `energy_usage`. If `burns_fluid` is `false`, `maximum_temperature` will also be used. If the attempt of the game to calculate this value fails (`scale_energy_usage` is `false` and a fluid box filter is set), then `scale_energy_usage` will be forced to `true`, to prevent the energy source from being an infinite fluid sink. More context [on the forums](https://forums.factorio.com/90613).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/FluidEnergySource.html%23fluid_usage_per_tick#fluid_usage_per_tick)
---@field fluid_usage_per_tick? FluidAmount
---@
